INSERT INTO public.journals (id, journable_type, journable_id, user_id, notes, created_at, version, updated_at, data_type, data_id, cause, validity_period, restricted) VALUES (59, 'WorkPackage', 44, 4, '### Case Determination / Call Recorded (As of 07/14/2025)

* **Written Response Filed:** `/DER_Program/Correspondence/ALN-108_PreApplication_Response.docx` (Doc no. `DER-CORR-ALN-108-2025-07-14`, Rev 1, dated `07/14/2025`; also saved at `/filesystem/ALN-108_PreApplication_Response.docx`).
* **Call on Request Item 1 (3.0 MW Capacity Confirmation on Feeder ALN-108):** **NOT CONFIRMED / DENIED as to 3.0 MW availability; CONFIRMED at `0.8 MW` (`800 kW`) current working interim netted available capacity as of `07/14/2025`.**
  * **Published Baseline (`HCM-2024-Q2`, published `05/15/2024`, Last Study Date `04/2024`):** **`3.0 MW`** (`3,000 kW`) on Feeder `ALN-108` (`Elderpine` substation, `13.2 kV`, `Pure Generation`).
  * **Pre-Publication Active Queue Entries on `ALN-108` (`2025-07-14_Active_Queue_Report.xlsx`, already reflected in the `04/2024` study / `05/15/2024` `3.0 MW` baseline):** **`PXA-2023-0894`** (`Ravenford Data Services` — `Ravenford Campus Rooftop PV`, **`1.1 MW`** [`1,100 kW`], queued `11/20/2023`, status: `ISA executed`) and **`PXA-2024-0091`** (`Fenwyn Industries Corp` — `Fenwyn Facility 3 Array`, **`690 kW`** [`0.69 MW`], queued `04/03/2024`, status: `construction`), subtotal **`1.79 MW`** (`1,790 kW`).
  * **Post-Publication Queue Addition 1 & Q3 2024 Interim Study (`PLN-ALN-108-2024-10`, dated `10/15/2024`):** **`PXA-2024-0231`** (`Grantwyck Solar LLC` — `Grantwyck ALN-108 Field Solar`, **`1.2 MW`** [`1,200 kW`], queued `09/18/2024`, status: `system impact study`). Netted in `PLN-ALN-108-2024-10` (`10/15/2024`) to reduce interim available capacity from `3.0 MW` to **`1.8 MW`** (`1,800 kW`).
  * **Post-Publication Queue Addition 2 (Subsequent to `10/15/2024`):** **`PXA-2025-0044`** (`Cindermere Renewables LLC` — `Cindermere Feeder Site A`, **`1.0 MW`** [`1,000 kW`], queued `02/06/2025`, status: `technical screening`). Total post-publication additions = **`2.2 MW`** (`2,200 kW`); total active queue on `ALN-108` = **4 projects totaling `3.99 MW` (`3,990 kW`)** (`0` on-hold or withdrawn projects).
  * **Current Working Interim Netted Available Capacity (`07/14/2025`):** `3.0 MW - 1.2 MW - 1.0 MW = 0.8 MW (800 kW)` (or `1.8 MW - 1.0 MW = 0.8 MW`). Northline Renewables'' requested `3.0 MW-AC` pure-generation project (`Elderpine Solar I`) exceeds remaining feeder headroom by **`2.2 MW` (`2,200 kW`)**.
* **Call on Request Item 2 (Advice to Requester — Conditions, Restrictions, Upgrade Indications & Sizing/POI Options):**
  * **Option A (Re-Scope / Control to `<= 0.8 MW` [`800 kW`] on `ALN-108`):** Reduce physical inverter nameplate to `<= 800 kW` (`DIS-01 Rev 4 §3.1`) or establish a recognized controlled export limit of `<= 800 kW` under **`DIS-01 Rev 4 §3.6`** by submitting both a valid **UL 1741 / UL 3141 PCS certification** and an approved **Control Narrative** (enforced via `TCS-02` SCADA telemetry and the utility POI recloser **ANSI 32 directional-power element** set to trip on violation). At `800 kW`, the project qualifies as Commercial Small-Scale DER (`500 kW – 1 MW`, `Tariff §12.2(a)`, `DIS-01 §3 Table 3-1` Category 2, eligible for `SRP-3 Rev 3` screening/supplemental review using daytime 10:00–16:00 AMI minimum-load data).
  * **Option B (Proceed at `3.0 MW` on `ALN-108` — Over-Subscribed by `2.2 MW`):** Processed in strict queue order (`Tariff §12.3` & `§12.7`) behind `PXA-2023-0894`, `PXA-2024-0091`, `PXA-2024-0231`, and `PXA-2025-0044`; classified as Medium-Scale DER (`1–5 MW`, `Tariff §12.2(b)`, `DIS-01 §3 Table 3-1` Category 3) requiring mandatory **System Impact Study (SIS)** and full feeder re-study, with expected thermal, voltage, protection, minimum-load, and/or Elderpine substation reverse-power upgrade costs unless senior queue entries withdraw or downsize.
  * **Option C (Evaluate Alternative Elderpine `13.2 kV` Pure-Generation Feeders `ALN-097` or `ALN-103`):** Adjacent Elderpine `13.2 kV` Pure-Generation feeders **`ALN-097`** (**`6.1 MW`** published available capacity on `HCM-2024-Q2`) and **`ALN-103`** (**`5.5 MW`** published available capacity on `HCM-2024-Q2`) have **`0 MW`** active or on-hold queue entries as of `07/14/2025`. POI and capacity selection must occur prior to ISA execution (`Tariff §12.6`, `DIS-01 Rev 4 §7`).
  * **Mandatory Technical & Lead-Time Advisories:** Requires `CEL-2025-Q2` (`04/30/2025`) certified inverters; utility-owned POI recloser (`DIS-01 Table 5-1`, `DPS-07 §4.2`, `ERP-9 §3` / `EB-2025-03` Precedents `ER-11-2025-004` & `ER-11-2025-009`); utility-owned RTU (`YOT-8963`, `YOT-8856`, or `YOT-7963`) with 4-hour UPS and live DNP3 SCADA telemetry prior to PTO (`TCS-02 §3.2`, `§3.4`, `§5`); and project schedule must accommodate the **`~8-month` supplier lead time** from `Kelvraith Grid Systems, Inc.` (RTUs) and `Norstead Power Controls, LLC` (POI reclosers) (`SCADA-EQP-2025-06`, deployed under `OG-17 Rev 1`) for the `Q4 2026` target.
* **Call on Request Item 3 (Pre-Application Dialogue Meeting):** **APPROVED / GRANTED.** Pre-application dialogue meeting offered with `June Halloway` (Distribution Planning), `Meera Vellanki` (Interconnection Studies), and `Ivo Grantham` (DER Planning Group).

---

### Required Follow-Up Actions Logged (Map Maintenance, Re-Study & Dialogue)

1. **Follow-Up 1 — Reissue / Supersede Interim Planning Study `PLN-ALN-108-2024-10` (Owner: `June Halloway`, Distribution Planning):** Per `PLN-ALN-108-2024-10 §5`, reissue/supersede the `10/15/2024` interim memorandum (`1.8 MW`) to incorporate `PXA-2025-0044` (`Cindermere Renewables LLC`, `1.0 MW`, queued `02/06/2025`) alongside `PXA-2024-0231` (`Grantwyck Solar LLC`, `1.2 MW`, queued `09/18/2024`), updating the working interim netted capacity of record on Feeder `ALN-108` to **`0.8 MW` (`800 kW`)**.
2. **Follow-Up 2 — Priority Hosting Capacity Map Refresh & Full Feeder `ALN-108` Planning Re-Study (Owners: `June Halloway`, Distribution Planning & `Ivo Grantham`, DER Planning Group):** `HCM-2024-Q2` (`05/15/2024`) is overdue on its quarterly refresh commitment by over four quarters. Per Regulatory Affairs Tasking Memo **`RA-2025-07-01 §3.7`** and `PLN-ALN-108-2024-10 §5`, Feeder `ALN-108` is flagged and scheduled for priority Hosting Capacity Map refresh and full feeder-level re-study under all three `HCM-2024-Q2` refresh prioritization criteria:
   * *(i) Application / Pre-Application Date:* Unreflected post-publication queue entries dating to `09/18/2024` (`PXA-2024-0231`) and `02/06/2025` (`PXA-2025-0044`), plus the `07/02/2025` pre-application request, against a `04/2024` baseline study.
   * *(ii) Capacity Requested Relative to Published Figure:* `2.2 MW` already queued post-publication (`73.33%` of the `3.0 MW` published baseline) plus `3.0 MW` requested by Northline (`100.0%` of published baseline; `5.2 MW` combined post-publication demand = `173.33%` of published baseline, or `375.0%` of remaining `0.8 MW` interim capacity).
   * *(iii) DER Category Weighting:* `Pure Generation` (front-of-the-meter, 100% export) carries the highest priority weighting against feeder headroom.
3. **Follow-Up 3 — Convene Pre-Application Dialogue Meeting with Northline Renewables LLC (Owners: `June Halloway`, `Meera Vellanki`, `Ivo Grantham`):** Meet with `Peter Ashford` (`Northline Renewables LLC`) to review the `0.8 MW` capacity calculation on `ALN-108`, `<= 800 kW` downsizing or `DIS-01 §3.6` PCS control narrative options vs. `3.0 MW` full SIS/upgrade path, and alternative Elderpine `13.2 kV` pure-generation feeders `ALN-097` (`6.1 MW`) and `ALN-103` (`5.5 MW`).
4. **Follow-Up 4 — Regulatory Affairs Reporting (`08/15/2025` League Response & `08/22/2025` / `09/10/2025` APUC Docket `APUC-2025-ER-014`):** Incorporate this `RA-2025-07-01 §3.7` hosting-capacity correction and `HCM-2024-Q2` priority refresh action into the weekly Friday backlog report (`RA-2025-07-01 §4`), the `08/15/2025` Alleron Municipal League response, and the APUC Information Request response (`ERD-IR-2025-07-014` Item 2 on hosting-capacity information sufficiency).', '2026-11-24 09:37:47.564038+00', 2, '2026-11-24 09:37:48.734595+00', 'Journal::WorkPackageJournal', 108, '{}', '["2026-11-24 09:37:47.564038+00",)', false);
