### Case Determination / Call Recorded (07/14/2025)

* **Written Response Filed:** `/DER_Program/Correspondence/ALN-108_PreApplication_Response.docx` (Doc no. `DER-CORR-ALN-108-2025-07-14`, Rev 1, dated `07/14/2025`; also saved at `/filesystem/ALN-108_PreApplication_Response.docx`).
* **Call on Request Item 1 (3.0 MW Available Capacity Confirmation on Feeder ALN-108):** **NOT CONFIRMED / DENIED as to 3.0 MW; CONFIRMED at `0.8 MW` (`800 kW`) current working interim netted available capacity as of `07/14/2025`.**
  * Published Hosting Capacity Map baseline (`HCM-2024-Q2`, published `05/15/2024`, Last Study Date `04/2024`): **`3.0 MW`** (`3,000 kW`) on Feeder `ALN-108` (`Elderpine` substation, `13.2 kV`, `Pure Generation`).
  * Pre-publication active queue entries on `ALN-108` (`2025-07-14_Active_Queue_Report.xlsx`, already accounted for in the `04/2024` study / `05/15/2024` `3.0 MW` baseline): **`PXA-2023-0894`** (`Ravenford Data Services` — `Ravenford Campus Rooftop PV`, `1.1 MW`, queued `11/20/2023`, status: `ISA executed`) and **`PXA-2024-0091`** (`Fenwyn Industries Corp` — `Fenwyn Facility 3 Array`, `690 kW` [`0.69 MW`], queued `04/03/2024`, status: `construction`), subtotal **`1.79 MW`** (`1,790 kW`).
  * Post-publication queue addition 1: **`PXA-2024-0231`** (`Grantwyck Solar LLC` — `Grantwyck ALN-108 Field Solar`, **`1.2 MW`** [`1,200 kW`], queued `09/18/2024`, status: `system impact study`), netted in Q3 2024 interim study `PLN-ALN-108-2024-10` (`10/15/2024`) to reduce interim capacity from `3.0 MW` to **`1.8 MW`** (`1,800 kW`).
  * Post-publication queue addition 2 (subsequent to `10/15/2024`): **`PXA-2025-0044`** (`Cindermere Renewables LLC` — `Cindermere Feeder Site A`, **`1.0 MW`** [`1,000 kW`], queued `02/06/2025`, status: `technical screening`). Total post-publication additions = **`2.2 MW`** (`2,200 kW`); total active queue on `ALN-108` = **4 projects totaling `3.99 MW` (`3,990 kW`)** (`0` on-hold or withdrawn).
  * **Current Netted Available Capacity (`07/14/2025`):** `3.0 MW - 1.2 MW - 1.0 MW = 0.8 MW (800 kW)` (a **`2.2 MW` [`2,200 kW`] shortfall** for Northline Renewables'' requested `3.0 MW-AC` `Elderpine Solar I` project).
* **Call on Request Item 2 (Requester Advisory — Conditions, Restrictions, Upgrade Indications & Sizing/POI Options):**
  * **(A) Re-Scope / Control on `ALN-108` to `<= 0.8 MW` (`800 kW` AC):** Reduce inverter nameplate to `<= 800 kW` (`DIS-01 Rev 4 §3.1`) or establish a recognized controlled export limit `<= 800 kW` under **`DIS-01 Rev 4 §3.6`** via both a valid **UL 1741 / UL 3141 PCS certification** and an approved **Control Narrative** (enforced via `TCS-02` SCADA telemetry and the utility POI recloser **ANSI 32 directional-power element**), placing the site in Commercial Small-Scale DER (`500 kW – 1 MW`, `Tariff §12.2(a)`, `DIS-01 Table 3-1` Category 2, eligible for `SRP-3 Rev 3` screening/supplemental review with 10:00–16:00 daytime AMI minimum load).
  * **(B) Proceed at `3.0 MW` on `ALN-108` (`2.2 MW` Over-Subscribed):** Queued behind `PXA-2023-0894`, `PXA-2024-0091`, `PXA-2024-0231`, and `PXA-2025-0044` (`Tariff §12.3` & `§12.7`); requires mandatory Medium-Scale **System Impact Study (SIS)** (`Tariff §12.2(b)`, `DIS-01 Table 3-1` Category 3) and full feeder re-study, with expected thermal, voltage, protection, minimum-load, and/or substation reverse-power upgrade costs unless senior queue entries withdraw or downsize.
  * **(C) Evaluate Alternative Elderpine `13.2 kV` Pure-Generation Feeders `ALN-097` (`6.1 MW` published, `0 MW` queued) or `ALN-103` (`5.5 MW` published, `0 MW` queued):** Must select POI and capacity prior to ISA execution (`Tariff §12.6`, `DIS-01 §7`).
  * **(D) Mandatory Technical & Schedule Conditions:** `CEL-2025-Q2` (`04/30/2025`) certified inverters; utility-owned POI recloser (`DIS-01 Table 5-1`, `DPS-07 §4.2`, `ERP-9 §3` / `EB-2025-03` Precedents `ER-11-2025-004` & `ER-11-2025-009`); utility-owned RTU (`YOT-8963`, `YOT-8856`, or `YOT-7963`) with 4-hour UPS and live DNP3 SCADA telemetry prior to PTO (`TCS-02 §3.2`, `§3.4`, `§5`); and **`~8-month` supplier lead time** (`Kelvraith Grid Systems, Inc.` / `Norstead Power Controls, LLC`, `SCADA-EQP-2025-06`, deployed under `OG-17 Rev 1`) for the `Q4 2026` target.
* **Call on Request Item 3 (Pre-Application Dialogue Meeting):** **APPROVED / GRANTED.** Offered with `June Halloway` (Distribution Planning), `Meera Vellanki` (Interconnection Studies), and `Ivo Grantham` (DER Planning Group).

### Required Follow-Up Logged

1. **Reissue / Supersede Interim Planning Study `PLN-ALN-108-2024-10` (Owner: `June Halloway`):** Per `PLN-ALN-108-2024-10 §5`, reissue/supersede the `10/15/2024` study (`1.8 MW`) to incorporate `PXA-2025-0044` (`1.0 MW`, queued `02/06/2025`) alongside `PXA-2024-0231` (`1.2 MW`, queued `09/18/2024`), updating the working interim netted capacity of record on Feeder `ALN-108` to **`0.8 MW` (`800 kW`)**.
2. **Priority Hosting Capacity Map Refresh & Full Feeder `ALN-108` Re-Study (Owners: `June Halloway` & `Ivo Grantham`):** `HCM-2024-Q2` (`05/15/2024`) is overdue on its quarterly refresh commitment by over four quarters. Flagged and requested under **`RA-2025-07-01 §3.7`** and all three `HCM-2024-Q2` refresh prioritization criteria: (1) application/pre-application date (`09/18/2024`, `02/06/2025`, `07/02/2025` against `04/2024` study), (2) requested capacity relative to published figure (`2.2 MW` queued = `73.33%` of `3.0 MW` published baseline; `3.0 MW` requested = `100.0%` of baseline / `375.0%` of `0.8 MW` remaining interim capacity; `5.2 MW` combined = `173.33%` of baseline), and (3) `Pure Generation` DER category weighting.
3. **Convene Pre-Application Dialogue Meeting with Northline Renewables (Owners: `June Halloway`, `Meera Vellanki`, `Ivo Grantham`):** Meet with `Peter Ashford` (`Northline Renewables LLC`) on `ALN-108` sizing (`<= 800 kW` / `DIS-01 §3.6` PCS control vs. `3.0 MW` SIS/upgrades) and alternative Elderpine `13.2 kV` feeders `ALN-097` (`6.1 MW`) and `ALN-103` (`5.5 MW`).
4. **Regulatory Affairs Reporting (`08/15/2025` League Response & `08/22/2025` / `09/10/2025` APUC Docket `APUC-2025-ER-014`):** Log completion of `RA-2025-07-01 §3.7` hosting-capacity correction and `HCM-2024-Q2` refresh status for the `08/15/2025` League response and APUC IR `ERD-IR-2025-07-014` Item 2.', '2025-08-15', NULL, 12, 9, 8, 5, 4, 1, 100, NULL, '2026-11-24 08:11:38.116109+00', '2026-11-24 09:37:48.734595+00', '2025-07-02', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, true, NULL, 33, false, NULL, NULL, NULL);
